{"name":"Star of Bethlehem","hex":"#f5eedc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Star of Bethlehem","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The bright star in the Gospel of Matthew that lead the \"wise men from the East\" to travel to Bethlehem."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Star_of_Bethlehem"}],"entries":[{"title":"Star of Bethlehem","blocks":[{"text":"The Star of Bethlehem, or Christmas Star, appears in the nativity of Jesus as accounted in the Gospel of Matthew chapter 2, where \"wise men from the East\" (Magi) are inspired by the star to travel to Jerusalem."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Giotto_-_Scrovegni_-_-18-_-_Adoration_of_the_Magi.jpg/330px-Giotto_-_Scrovegni_-_-18-_-_Adoration_of_the_Magi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_of_Bethlehem","wikidata":"Q211221"},{"title":"Star of Bethlehem (painting)","blocks":[{"text":"The Star of Bethlehem is a painting in watercolour by Sir Edward Burne-Jones depicting the Adoration of the Magi with an angel holding the star of Bethlehem. It was commissioned by the Corporation of the City of Birmingham for its new Museum and Art Gallery in 1887, two years after Burne-Jones was elected Honorary President of the Royal Birmingham Society of Artists. At 101+1⁄8 by 152 inches, The Star of Bethlehem was the largest watercolour of the 19th century. It was completed in 1890 and was first exhibited in 1891."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Edward_Burne-Jones_Star_of_Bethlehem.jpg/330px-Edward_Burne-Jones_Star_of_Bethlehem.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_of_Bethlehem_(painting)","wikidata":"Q7601237"},{"title":"Star","blocks":[{"text":"A star is a luminous spheroid of plasma held together by self-gravity. The nearest star to Earth is the Sun. Many other stars are visible to the naked eye at night; their immense distances from Earth make them appear as fixed points of light. The most prominent stars have been categorised into constellations and asterisms, and many of the brightest stars have proper names. Astronomers have assembled star catalogues that identify the known stars and provide standardized stellar designations. The observable universe contains an estimated 1022 to 1024 stars. Only about 4,000 of these stars are visible to the naked eye—all within the Milky Way galaxy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star","wikidata":"Q523"},{"title":"Bethlehem","blocks":[{"text":"Bethlehem is a city in the West Bank, Palestine, located about ten kilometres south of Jerusalem, and the capital of the Bethlehem Governorate. It had a population of 28,591 people, as of 2017. The city's economy is strongly linked to tourism, especially during the Christmas period, when Christians embark on a pilgrimage to the Church of the Nativity, which is revered as the location of the birth of Jesus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Church_of_the_Nativity_%287703592746%29.jpg/330px-Church_of_the_Nativity_%287703592746%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bethlehem","wikidata":"Q5776"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/L_Adoration_des_Mages.jpg/330px-L_Adoration_des_Mages.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/L_Adoration_des_Mages.jpg/330px-L_Adoration_des_Mages.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Adoration of the Magi, by Jean Fouquet (15th century). The Star of Bethlehem can be seen in the top right. The soldiers and castle in the background may represent the Battle of Castillon (1453).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AL_Adoration_des_Mages.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Sky_Jerusalem_South-7BC-11-12.gif/500px-Sky_Jerusalem_South-7BC-11-12.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Sky_Jerusalem_South-7BC-11-12.gif/500px-Sky_Jerusalem_South-7BC-11-12.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jerusalem sky on November 12, 7 BC.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASky_Jerusalem_South-7BC-11-12.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Beit_alfa01.jpg/500px-Beit_alfa01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Beit_alfa01.jpg/500px-Beit_alfa01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A zodiac from a 6th-century mosaic at a synagogue in Beit Alpha, Israel","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeit_alfa01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Ravenna_Basilica_of_Sant%27Apollinare_Nuovo_3_Wise_men.jpg/500px-Ravenna_Basilica_of_Sant%27Apollinare_Nuovo_3_Wise_men.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Ravenna_Basilica_of_Sant%27Apollinare_Nuovo_3_Wise_men.jpg/1280px-Ravenna_Basilica_of_Sant%27Apollinare_Nuovo_3_Wise_men.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Ravenna_Basilica_of_Sant%27Apollinare_Nuovo_3_Wise_men.jpg/500px-Ravenna_Basilica_of_Sant%27Apollinare_Nuovo_3_Wise_men.jpg?utm_source=